Application Definition with Git
Objectives
Design and deploy a containerized application to Kubernetes using raw manifests and a Helm chart managed entirely through a local Git repository
Configure Argo CD to watch the Git repository and automatically reconcile cluster state with declared configuration
Demonstrate a GitOps update cycle by committing a version change and verifying Argo CD propagates it to the cluster without manual kubectl intervention
Prerequisites
Comfort with Linux command-line operations including file editing, process management, and reading command output
Conceptual understanding of containers, Kubernetes workloads (Deployment, Service), and version control with Git
Lab Environment
You will work on a dedicated AWS EC2 Ubuntu instance provided by Al Nafi. The instance has a base Ubuntu installation; you will install all required tools in Task 1.

Task 1: Install and Verify the Full Toolchain
Requirement 1
Install Docker, kubectl, Helm, kind (Kubernetes-in-Docker), and the Argo CD CLI on the bare Ubuntu instance. Create a single-node kind cluster named gitops-lab, deploy Argo CD into it, and confirm every component reaches a healthy state before proceeding.

